Version 4
SHEET 1 880 680
WIRE 0 96 112 96
WIRE 160 80 240 80
FLAG 0 176 0
FLAG 112 144 0
FLAG 160 160 0
FLAG 240 160 0
FLAG 0 96 in
FLAG 240 80 out
SYMBOL voltage 0 80 R0
SYMATTR InstName V1
SYMATTR Value PULSE(0 1 1m 1u 1u 10m 20m) AC 1
SYMBOL e 160 64 R0
SYMATTR InstName E1
SYMATTR Value Laplace=1/(1+s*tau)
SYMBOL res 224 64 R0
SYMATTR InstName R1
SYMATTR Value 1k
TEXT -32 232 Left 2 !.param tau=1m
TEXT -32 256 Left 2 !.ac dec 20 1 10k
TEXT -32 280 Left 2 ;.tran 6m
TEXT -32 304 Left 2 !.meas ac fc WHEN vdb(out)=-3
TEXT -32 352 Left 2 ;A Laplace source: E1's output is its input through H(s) = 1/(1+s*tau), a first-order
TEXT -32 376 Left 2 ;low-pass with fc = 1/(2*pi*tau) = 159 Hz (the AC tab). The Transient tab shows its step
TEXT -32 400 Left 2 ;response, 1 - exp(-t/tau). Any ratio of polynomials in s works, with parameters in it.
